      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case is reported in which simultaneous surgical correction of coronary atherosclerosis and cholelithiasis was performed. A 71-year-old man was admitted with severe stable angina and right hypochondrial dull pain. Coronary angiograms disclosed severe triple vessel disease, and abdominal echography demonstrated gallstone. He underwent bypass of left anterior descending, diagonal, obtuse marginal, and right coronary arteries with autogenous saphenous vein on cardiopulmonary bypass. The procedure was followed immediately by cholecystectomy. His postoperative course was uneventful."},
